{"id":"a4901c0343d9dbe4","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-df-torus-decomposition.md","title":"Torus-Cutting Decomposition","display":"df-torus-decomposition — Torus-Cutting Decomposition","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-torus-decomposition","aliases":["58-df-torus-decomposition","Toroidal Decomposition"],"display":"df-torus-decomposition — Torus-Cutting Decomposition","depends_on":["[[../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md]]","[[../batch10/58-df-connected.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-finite.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-torus-decomposition"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-torus-decomposition</span><span>Toroidal Decomposition</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-torus-decomposition — Torus-Cutting Decomposition"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"71801f5b9407391a\" href=\"?note=71801f5b9407391a\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-connected.md\">../batch10/58-df-connected.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c4b4a825f2ea608d\" href=\"?note=c4b4a825f2ea608d\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md\">../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"d9a25b0ac94a3598\" href=\"?note=d9a25b0ac94a3598\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-finite.md\">../batch04/58-df-finite.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,\\tau_M,\\mathcal T,\\mathcal P\\in V\">\\(M,\\tau_M,\\mathcal T,\\mathcal P\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb T^2,\\tau_{\\mathbb T^2}\\in V\">\\(\\mathbb T^2,\\tau_{\\mathbb T^2}\\in V\\)</span>（标准拓扑二维环面）</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_M\\!\\upharpoonright A\\coloneqq\\{U\\cap A:U\\in\\tau_M\\}\">\\(\\tau_M\\!\\upharpoonright A\\coloneqq\\{U\\cap A:U\\in\\tau_M\\}\\)</span>（子空间拓扑）</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TopologicalSpace}_S,\\mathrm{Connected}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{TopologicalSpace}_S,\\mathrm{Connected}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"71801f5b9407391a\" href=\"?note=71801f5b9407391a\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-connected.md\">../batch10/58-df-connected.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Homeo}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Homeo}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Finite}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Finite}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"c4b4a825f2ea608d\" href=\"?note=c4b4a825f2ea608d\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md\">../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"d9a25b0ac94a3598\" href=\"?note=d9a25b0ac94a3598\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-finite.md\">../batch04/58-df-finite.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TorusDecomposition}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{TorusDecomposition}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (本文件定义)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}torus\\text{-}decomposition}\\vdash{}&amp;\\mathrm{TorusDecomposition}_S(M,\\tau_M,\\mathcal T,\\mathcal P)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{TopologicalSpace}_S(M,\\tau_M)\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(\\mathcal T)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A\\in\\mathcal T\\;\\Bigl(A\\subseteq M\\land\\exists h\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(h,A,\\tau_M\\!\\upharpoonright A,\\mathbb T^2,\\tau_{\\mathbb T^2})\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A,B\\in\\mathcal T\\;(A\\neq B\\to A\\cap B=\\emptyset)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathcal P=\\Bigl\\{C\\subseteq M\\setminus\\bigcup\\mathcal T:\\mathrm{Connected}_S(C,\\tau_M\\!\\upharpoonright C)\\land\\neg\\exists D\\in V\\;\\bigl(C\\subsetneq D\\subseteq M\\setminus\\bigcup\\mathcal T\\land\\mathrm{Connected}_S(D,\\tau_M\\!\\upharpoonright D)\\bigr)\\Bigr\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}torus\\text{-}decomposition}\\vdash{}&amp;\\mathrm{TorusDecomposition}_S(M,\\tau_M,\\mathcal T,\\mathcal P)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{TopologicalSpace}_S(M,\\tau_M)\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(\\mathcal T)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A\\in\\mathcal T\\;\\Bigl(A\\subseteq M\\land\\exists h\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(h,A,\\tau_M\\!\\upharpoonright A,\\mathbb T^2,\\tau_{\\mathbb T^2})\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A,B\\in\\mathcal T\\;(A\\neq B\\to A\\cap B=\\emptyset)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathcal P=\\Bigl\\{C\\subseteq M\\setminus\\bigcup\\mathcal T:\\mathrm{Connected}_S(C,\\tau_M\\!\\upharpoonright C)\\land\\neg\\exists D\\in V\\;\\bigl(C\\subsetneq D\\subseteq M\\setminus\\bigcup\\mathcal T\\land\\mathrm{Connected}_S(D,\\tau_M\\!\\upharpoonright D)\\bigr)\\Bigr\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This predicate records the topological cutting operation and its connected pieces. In a <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"3\">\\(3\\)</span>-manifold, a JSJ decomposition additionally requires the tori to be essential and a canonical minimal family.</li>\n<li>The assertion that the resulting prime/JSJ pieces support Thurston geometries is the geometrization theorem, not part of the definition of a torus cutting.</li>\n<li>Application: classify 3-manifolds</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Scott, The Geometries of 3-Manifolds</li>\n<li>Thurston, Three-Dimensional Geometry and Topology</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"815e63e5071e7b58","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-connected.md","status":"resolved","id":"71801f5b9407391a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-df-connected.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md","status":"resolved","id":"c4b4a825f2ea608d","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-finite.md","status":"resolved","id":"d9a25b0ac94a3598","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-finite.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"815e63e5071e7b58","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{TopologicalSpace}_S,\\mathrm{Connected}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md]] and [[../batch10/58-df-connected.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-connected.md","status":"resolved","id":"